WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.689
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Saturday, October twenty-fourth.

2
00:00:04.689 --> 00:00:07.593
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.593 --> 00:00:10.883
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:10.883 --> 00:00:12.236
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:12.236 --> 00:00:24.283
Washington is thinning embassy staff across the Middle East after an intelligence warning about Iranian plots, occupied Crimea lost power and most internet overnight, and Jordan remains on alert after the church attack in Karak.

6
00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:27.070
Here's the detail.

7
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:28.418
What changed.

8
00:00:28.418 --> 00:00:34.542
In the Middle East, the State Department has updated its travel advisories across the region, citing Houthi attacks it says could escalate rapidly.

9
00:00:34.542 --> 00:00:37.826
The National counts thirteen countries.

10
00:00:37.826 --> 00:00:45.609
The Associated Press reports the State Department is reducing staff at the US embassies in Jordan, Lebanon, Qatar and the United Arab Emirates.

11
00:00:45.609 --> 00:00:48.931
Those embassies stay open, and staff are not ordered to leave.

12
00:00:48.931 --> 00:00:52.513
Saudi Arabia has been under an ordered departure for non-emergency staff and families since Wednesday.

13
00:00:52.513 --> 00:01:03.356
The AP and the Critical Threats Project report a memo from the Director of National Intelligence saying Iranian plots against US personnel have reached advanced stages in the Middle East and other countries.

14
00:01:03.356 --> 00:01:09.367
Status: the advisories and staffing changes are confirmed by the State Department.

15
00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.366
The memo's detail comes through press reporting.

16
00:01:10.366 --> 00:01:20.257
If you have people in the Gulf, Jordan or Lebanon: confirm contact lists and shelter plans, and agree now on what would trigger a move.

17
00:01:20.257 --> 00:01:27.027
In occupied Crimea, NetBlocks and Cloudflare Radar report internet connectivity largely knocked out after the power failed overnight, with traffic down more than eighty percent.

18
00:01:27.027 --> 00:01:37.745
Crimea's Russian-installed head, Sergei Aksyonov, says power and water are now being rationed across the peninsula, Radio Free Europe and Russian state media report.

19
00:01:37.745 --> 00:01:42.786
In Sevastopol, officials say only about forty percent of mobile base stations are working.

20
00:01:42.786 --> 00:01:51.124
Russian-installed officials blame a drone attack on the grid outside Crimea, and NetBlocks links it to Ukrainian drone strikes on the Taman substation in southern Russia.

21
00:01:51.124 --> 00:01:53.700
Officials in Sevastopol give no date for full restoration.

22
00:01:53.700 --> 00:02:00.734
The Critical Threats Project says the same overnight strikes also cut power across other occupied parts of Ukraine.

23
00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:05.580
In Jordan, Reuters now puts the death toll from Friday's church attack in Karak governorate at eight.

24
00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:14.278
The US Embassy says security has been ramped up, and the State Department says the area around the church is cordoned off while the hunt for the attackers goes on.

25
00:02:14.278 --> 00:02:17.297
Status: confirmed by Jordanian officials.

26
00:02:17.297 --> 00:02:19.490
No verified claim of responsibility.

27
00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.604
Plan for checkpoints and delays.

28
00:02:22.604 --> 00:02:23.104
Operations check.

29
00:02:23.104 --> 00:02:27.294
Airspace and aviation: Houthi strikes on Saudi airports in recent weeks have disrupted flights.

30
00:02:27.294 --> 00:02:38.608
The National reports Riyadh's main airport has only partly reopened, and Saudi aviation authorities said on Wednesday that the latest strike, on Dammam's airport, killed two.

31
00:02:38.608 --> 00:02:44.749
The Houthis now claim new attacks on three Saudi airports and on oil sites at Saudi Red Sea ports, the Critical Threats Project reports.

32
00:02:44.749 --> 00:02:45.680
That is the group's own claim.

33
00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:54.492
Shipping: Reuters reports attacks on ships in the Strait of Hormuz hit a record in October, and Lloyd's List says crude tanker rates are now easing after the spike.

34
00:02:54.492 --> 00:03:00.387
In the Black Sea, the Critical Threats Project says a likely Russian drone struck a cargo ship off Romania on Friday.

35
00:03:00.387 --> 00:03:02.036
Internet and telecom: Crimea, as above.

36
00:03:02.036 --> 00:03:13.059
In Ukraine, President Zelenskyy says Starlink and Starshield service is back to normal after speed restrictions, Radio Free Europe reports, and Ukrainian officials now confirm unrestricted access.

37
00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:16.931
Power: Crimea, and Typhoon Champi cut power in parts of Taiwan, Reuters reports.

38
00:03:16.931 --> 00:03:19.105
Borders: no new country-wide closures.

39
00:03:19.105 --> 00:03:24.763
The security cordon in Karak and the demolitions in Hebron are the local constraints to watch.

40
00:03:24.763 --> 00:03:29.979
Cyber: CISA says organizations that can't patch the PHP2Shell flaw should take affected PHP systems offline until they can.

41
00:03:29.979 --> 00:03:42.502
In the West Bank, Reuters reports Israeli forces demolished homes and damaged roads in Hebron, forcing about twelve hundred Palestinians to leave, a day after an attack killed two Israeli soldiers.

42
00:03:42.502 --> 00:03:43.399
Look-ahead.

43
00:03:43.399 --> 00:03:45.562
Brazil's presidential runoff is tomorrow.

44
00:03:45.562 --> 00:03:53.096
A limited humanitarian ceasefire in occupied Oleshky, in Ukraine's Kherson region, is due to start October twenty seventh, though its terms remain unclear.

45
00:03:53.096 --> 00:03:56.994
China's Communist Party meets October twenty sixth to twenty ninth.

46
00:03:56.994 --> 00:03:58.889
Israelis vote next week.

47
00:03:58.889 --> 00:04:04.052
Canada warns demonstrations in Tanzania around October twenty ninth can turn violent.

48
00:04:04.052 --> 00:04:06.871
US midterm elections are November third.

49
00:04:06.871 --> 00:04:08.313
That's today's brief.

50
00:04:08.313 --> 00:04:10.988
Current as of six thirty p.m.

51
00:04:10.988 --> 00:04:11.488
Central, Saturday.

52
00:04:11.488 --> 00:04:13.346
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

53
00:04:13.346 --> 00:04:17.866
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

54
00:04:17.866 --> 00:04:20.210
Check the original source before you act.

55
00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.108
Questions?

56
00:04:21.108 --> 00:04:24.709
Reach Tueri at contact at tuerisystems dot com.

57
00:04:24.709 --> 00:04:25.942
Thanks for listening.
